how about this also: a wizard has a higher probability of finding magic
because, as you say, the probability of generation of magic goes up for
him (with a corresponding decrease in weapon generation, etc.) and
monsters that can, also tend to use (and be generated with) more magic
against the wizard.  this turns the wizards game more into a magic arena.
however, a wizard shouldn't be entirely loath to carrying a +11 Sunsword.
to the extent that this is possible other differences should apply to
the other character classes (altho the big difference tends to be fighter
vs. magic user).

[] This is not realistic at all, but I can't think of any better solution.

well, i like to think that realism is a weak crutch (i.e. we can't lean
on it too heavily else it will break).  realism is needed to the extent
that the game remains comprehensible.  what is far more important is
playability (in my opinion).  perhaps you can develop the idea that
games for different character types should be significantly different?

